# Who is who in the git history: one name and one GitHub address per person.
#
# The page footer (contributors with avatars and shares) reads names through this file,
# and so do `git log` and `git blame`. It merges a person's different commit e-mails and
# replaces GitHub handles with full names. The avatar comes from the GitHub no-reply
# address (id+login@users.noreply.github.com).
#
# Format: Full Name <id+login@users.noreply.github.com> <e-mail used in commits>
# A line without a second address only sets the name for that address.
# New contributor with a handle as name or a second e-mail? Add a line here. The GitHub
# account behind an e-mail: gh api repos/HOPLAB-LBP/hoplab-wiki/commits/<sha> -q .author

